    Messages carry a monotonically increasing sequence number per account.
    A message is applied only when its sequence is exactly the next expected
    sequence for that account. Redeliveries and stale (older) messages are
    dropped, while messages that arrive ahead of a gap are held until the
    missing sequence arrives, at which point they flush in order.
